1255
00:53:03.250 --> 00:53:04.110
I remember it differently.
我的记忆却不太一样。

1256
00:53:04.370 --> 00:53:07.250
Even Phyllis, when she said, I have two things to say.
就连菲利斯说那句“我有两件事要说”的时候也是。

1257
00:53:07.350 --> 00:53:08.490
First thing is I love you.
第一件事是我爱你。

1258
00:53:09.250 --> 00:53:09.890
No, no, no.
不，不，不。

1259
00:53:09.990 --> 00:53:15.830
So I should say some of it was scripted, but we did also improvise some.
所以我应该说，其中一部分是有剧本的，但我们也确实进行了一些即兴发挥。

1260
00:53:15.970 --> 00:53:16.270
Okay.
好吧。

1261
00:53:16.410 --> 00:53:17.090
So it was both.
所以两者都有。

1262
00:53:17.250 --> 00:53:18.710
And that happened a lot when we were shooting.
我们在拍摄时经常发生这种情况。

1263
00:53:18.890 --> 00:53:22.950
They would leave the cameras rolling, and then we would throw stuff out there.
他们会让摄像机一直开着，然后我们就随性发挥。

1264
00:53:23.050 --> 00:53:25.410
And some of the improvisations stayed in.
有些即兴表演的内容被保留了下来。

1265
00:53:25.510 --> 00:53:26.250
I love that.
我喜欢这样。

1266
00:53:26.350 --> 00:53:30.010
But you could definitely tell the beginning of the scene was scripted, getting you into it.
但你绝对能看出来场景的开头是有剧本的，是为了把你带入情境。

1267
00:53:30.110 --> 00:53:30.810
Yes, that's true.
是的，没错。

1268
00:53:31.010 --> 00:53:35.690
Back at Chili's, guys, let's have a little bit of an adult beverage time code count.
回到Chili's餐厅，伙计们，让我们来统计一下成人饮料的时间码。

1269
00:53:35.830 --> 00:53:36.270
Oh, dear.
噢，天哪。

1270
00:53:36.270 --> 00:53:40.610
So at 7 minutes, 59 seconds, Jan orders a vodka tonic.
在7分59秒时，简点了一杯伏特加汤力水。

1271
00:53:40.750 --> 00:53:42.490
We never see this vodka tonic.
我们从没见过这杯伏特加汤力水。

1272
00:53:42.750 --> 00:53:43.710
Oh, that's right.
噢，对哦。

1273
00:53:43.950 --> 00:53:44.070
Yeah.
是啊。

1274
00:53:44.390 --> 00:53:47.350
At 8 minutes, 35 seconds, they all have margaritas.
在8分35秒时，他们都喝上了玛格丽特。

1275
00:53:47.930 --> 00:53:50.210
So is Jan on her second drink?
所以简是在喝第二杯酒吗？

1276
00:53:50.510 --> 00:53:53.950
At 13 minutes, 44 seconds, Michael and Christian are having beers.
在13分44秒时，迈克尔和克里斯蒂安在喝啤酒。

1277
00:53:54.410 --> 00:53:56.630
Jan looks like she's having a water with lime.
简看起来像是在喝加青柠的水。

1278
00:53:56.730 --> 00:53:57.270
I can't tell.
我看不出来。

1279
00:53:57.410 --> 00:53:58.490
It's in a tall glass.
那是在一个高脚杯里。

1280
00:53:58.670 --> 00:54:00.830
Maybe that's finally her vodka tonic.
也许那终于就是她的伏特加汤力水了。

1281
00:54:00.910 --> 00:54:01.550
I don't know.
我不知道。

1282
00:54:01.750 --> 00:54:05.370
That's our adult beverage count for those of you who love the background stuff like me.
这就是我们的成人饮料统计，献给那些像我一样喜欢关注背景细节的观众。

1283
00:54:05.370 --> 00:54:08.230
Angela, I'm ready to take us on a date.
安吉拉，我准备好带我们去约会了。

1284
00:54:08.410 --> 00:54:09.070
To the roof.
去屋顶。

1285
00:54:09.250 --> 00:54:09.810
To the roof.
去屋顶。

1286
00:54:10.010 --> 00:54:11.890
Pam and Jim's roof date.
帕姆和吉姆的屋顶约会。

1287
00:54:12.210 --> 00:54:13.330
I have so many questions.
我有好多问题。

1288
00:54:13.750 --> 00:54:16.050
I have so many technical questions.
我有好多技术层面的问题。

1289
00:54:16.250 --> 00:54:16.410
Okay.
好吧。

1290
00:54:16.410 --> 00:54:19.930
And then I have some just, you know, fan of the office questions.
然后我还有一些，你知道的，作为《办公室》粉丝的问题。

1291
00:54:20.010 --> 00:54:20.610
What do you want to know?
你想知道什么？

1292
00:54:20.870 --> 00:54:22.310
How did you get up on that roof?
你们是怎么爬上那个屋顶的？

1293
00:54:22.470 --> 00:54:22.810
Okay.
好吧。

1294
00:54:22.810 --> 00:54:28.070
So the ladder that you see in the episode really leads up to the roof.
剧集里看到的那个梯子确实是通往屋顶的。

1295
00:54:28.210 --> 00:54:30.970
You really climbed that little fire escape looking ladder?
你们真的爬了那个看起来像消防通道的小梯子吗？

1296
00:54:31.170 --> 00:54:32.310
John and I did not.
约翰和我没有。

1297
00:54:32.490 --> 00:54:34.250
But that is how the crew got up there.
但那是剧组人员上去的方式。

1298
00:54:34.450 --> 00:54:34.670
Okay.
好吧。

1299
00:54:35.170 --> 00:54:38.090
John and I, for I guess...
约翰和我，我猜是因为……

1300
00:54:38.090 --> 00:54:38.890
Safety reasons?
安全原因？

1301
00:54:38.890 --> 00:54:42.770
And insurance reasons, we got into a harness.
出于保险考虑，我们系上了安全带。

1302
00:54:42.970 --> 00:54:43.550
Okay.
好的。

1303
00:54:43.910 --> 00:54:47.150
And then they lifted us up to the roof.
然后他们把我们吊到了屋顶上。

1304
00:54:47.390 --> 00:54:49.070
Like in a forklift kind of thing?
就像叉车那样的东西吗？

1305
00:54:49.110 --> 00:54:49.410
Yeah.
是的。

1306
00:54:49.630 --> 00:54:56.390
In some sort of weird platformy forklift, which seemed scarier and more dangerous than
是一种奇怪的平台式叉车，看起来比

1307
00:54:56.390 --> 00:54:58.470
if I'd just been allowed to use the ladder.
让我直接爬梯子上去还要吓人、还要危险。

1308
00:54:58.670 --> 00:55:04.290
And we shot on the actual roof of Dunder Mifflin, of the Dunder Mifflin building.
我们是在邓德·米夫林大楼真正的屋顶上拍摄的。

1309
00:55:04.510 --> 00:55:05.170
I would rather climb the ladder.
我宁愿爬梯子。

1310
00:55:05.490 --> 00:55:06.010
Same.
我也是。

1311
00:55:06.010 --> 00:55:11.830
I asked to climb the ladder, but we went up and down on the platform forklift.
我申请过爬梯子，但我们还是坐那个平台叉车上上下下。

1312
00:55:12.030 --> 00:55:12.310
Okay.
好吧。

1313
00:55:14.030 --> 00:55:15.950
I have a fan question about the roof.
我有一个关于屋顶的粉丝提问。

1314
00:55:16.310 --> 00:55:16.830
Okay.
好的。

1315
00:55:17.050 --> 00:55:17.690
James K.
James K.

1316
00:55:18.010 --> 00:55:19.690
asked, was it cold on the roof?
问，屋顶上冷吗？

1317
00:55:19.870 --> 00:55:20.870
It looked cold.
看起来挺冷的。

1318
00:55:21.030 --> 00:55:21.810
It wasn't.
并不冷。

1319
00:55:22.030 --> 00:55:22.850
It wasn't?
真的吗？

1320
00:55:22.910 --> 00:55:28.990
Oh, Angela, shooting the scene is one of my fondest memories of all time from the show.
噢，安吉拉，拍摄那场戏是我在剧组最美好的回忆之一。

1321
00:55:28.990 --> 00:55:37.230
Because the only people on the roof were me, John, Greg Daniels, Paul Lieberstein, our first
因为屋顶上只有我、约翰、格雷格·丹尼尔斯、保罗·利伯斯坦、我们的第一副导演，

1322
00:55:37.230 --> 00:55:40.690
AD, and our camera operator and DP, Randall Einhorn.
还有我们的摄像师和摄影指导兰德尔·艾因霍恩。

1323
00:55:41.410 --> 00:55:42.710
It was warm.
天气很暖和。

1324
00:55:42.870 --> 00:55:45.030
It was a warm summer evening.
那是一个温暖的夏夜。

1325
00:55:45.230 --> 00:55:46.710
But like a beautiful summer night.
就像一个美好的夏夜。

1326
00:55:47.070 --> 00:55:48.310
Warm breeze.
微风习习。

1327
00:55:49.610 --> 00:55:57.710
It was, I can't explain it, but this little group of us up on the roof, it hit me while
我没法解释，但我们那一小群人在屋顶上时，我突然意识到，

1328
00:55:57.710 --> 00:55:58.510
I was up there.
我当时就在那儿。

1329
00:55:59.470 --> 00:56:01.010
I'm on a TV show.
我在拍电视剧。

1330
00:56:01.030 --> 00:56:02.550
I'm living my dream.
我在实现我的梦想。

1331
00:56:03.510 --> 00:56:05.010
This is amazing.
这太棒了。

1332
00:56:05.390 --> 00:56:05.790
Right.
没错。

1333
00:56:05.950 --> 00:56:07.530
I'm sure it felt really magical.
我敢肯定那感觉一定很神奇。

1334
00:56:07.910 --> 00:56:09.170
Just like a magical moment.
就像一个神奇的时刻。

1335
00:56:09.170 --> 00:56:10.550
Completely magical.
完全是神奇的。

1336
00:56:10.550 --> 00:56:13.290
We had really gelled as a group at this point.
那时我们整个团队已经非常有默契了。

1337
00:56:13.550 --> 00:56:15.450
You know, we were really in it all together.
你知道，我们真的齐心协力。

1338
00:56:15.450 --> 00:56:18.110
We all loved the show so much.
我们所有人都非常热爱这部剧。

1339
00:56:18.390 --> 00:56:20.990
We loved being at work so much.
我们非常热爱这份工作。

1340
00:56:21.170 --> 00:56:23.490
It was just really, really special.
那段时光真的很特别。

1341
00:56:23.750 --> 00:56:26.890
And the grilled cheese sandwiches tasted so good.
而且烤奶酪三明治味道好极了。

1342
00:56:27.650 --> 00:56:28.670
It was great.
太棒了。

1343
00:56:28.890 --> 00:56:30.450
I have another fan question.
我还有另一个粉丝提问。

1344
00:56:30.610 --> 00:56:33.330
Donna asked, was anyone hurt by the fireworks?
唐娜问，有人被烟花炸伤吗？

1345
00:56:33.550 --> 00:56:34.650
That looked kind of dangerous.
那看起来有点危险。

1346
00:56:35.350 --> 00:56:39.090
So I saw Brian Baumgartner recently, and I asked him about,
我最近见到了布莱恩·鲍姆加特纳，我问了他关于，

1347
00:56:39.170 --> 00:56:42.930
the fireworks, he said, Jenna, it was insane.
烟花的事，他说，珍娜，那简直疯了。

1348
00:56:44.090 --> 00:56:48.090
There was no stunt coordinator for these fireworks.
放烟花的时候根本没有特技协调员。

1349
00:56:48.230 --> 00:56:55.470
He said, because they had to get the shot of us from so far away, they really left the
他说，因为他们必须从很远的地方拍我们，所以他们真的把

1350
00:56:55.470 --> 00:56:59.630
two of them out in the middle of this parking lot field alone.
他们俩单独留在了停车场那片空地的中央。

1351
00:56:59.630 --> 00:57:01.750
Which looked very dry.
看起来非常干燥。

1352
00:57:02.190 --> 00:57:02.430
Yeah.
是啊。

1353
00:57:02.670 --> 00:57:05.070
Well, you know, fireworks are illegal in LA.
嗯，你知道，在洛杉矶放烟花是违法的。

1354
00:57:05.350 --> 00:57:05.770
Oh my gosh.
天哪。

1355
00:57:05.770 --> 00:57:08.890
They had a hard time even getting fireworks for this scene.
他们为了拍这场戏，连搞到烟花都费了很大劲。

1356
00:57:08.890 --> 00:57:10.070
We were breaking the law?
我们当时在违法吗？

1357
00:57:10.270 --> 00:57:11.230
I'm not sure.
我不确定。

1358
00:57:11.730 --> 00:57:19.330
I know BJ said once in an article that there was a rule about how big the fireworks could
我知道BJ有次在文章里说过，关于烟花的大小有规定，

1359
00:57:19.330 --> 00:57:19.510
be.
不能太大。

1360
00:57:19.610 --> 00:57:23.650
They weren't allowed to shoot anything up in the air because LA is very dry.
他们不被允许往空中发射任何东西，因为洛杉矶非常干燥。

1361
00:57:23.890 --> 00:57:24.430
That's right.
没错。

1362
00:57:24.510 --> 00:57:25.570
I think I do know that.
我想我确实知道这一点。

1363
00:57:25.690 --> 00:57:27.310
So you can do the thing that's on the ground.
所以你们只能玩那种在地上的烟花。

1364
00:57:27.310 --> 00:57:27.570
Yeah.
是啊。

1365
00:57:27.630 --> 00:57:28.450
But that's it.
但也仅限于此。

1366
00:57:28.570 --> 00:57:28.750
Yes.
是的。

1367
00:57:28.890 --> 00:57:31.010
So they were like the sparkler thing on the ground.
所以它们就像是在地上那种会喷火花的烟花。

1368
00:57:31.210 --> 00:57:31.490
Yes.
是的。

1369
00:57:31.770 --> 00:57:37.250
And Brian said that they couldn't hear anything.
布莱恩说他们当时什么都听不见。

1370
00:57:37.250 --> 00:57:39.470
They could barely hear action or cut.
他们几乎听不到“开始”或“停”的指令。

1371
00:57:39.690 --> 00:57:42.110
They just were out there playing in these fireworks.
他们就在那儿玩着烟花。

1372
00:57:42.270 --> 00:57:46.830
But at a certain point, he heard someone shout, hop over them!
但在某个时刻，他听到有人大喊：跳过去！

1373
00:57:47.350 --> 00:57:48.310
Kick them!
踢开它们！

1374
00:57:49.350 --> 00:57:50.730
Like stuff like that.
诸如此类的话。

1375
00:57:50.850 --> 00:57:51.970
It was probably Greg.
那人可能是格雷格。

1376
00:57:51.970 --> 00:57:52.550
Like screaming.
就像在尖叫一样。

1377
00:57:53.590 --> 00:57:56.710
But Brian said they were just – it felt very real.
但布莱恩说他们当时只是——感觉非常真实。

1378
00:57:56.770 --> 00:58:01.790
And I think that was part of it about what made that night so magical was that it was
我觉得这也是那一晚如此神奇的原因之一，因为那感觉真的就像我们看着那帮家伙在玩烟花。

1379
00:58:01.790 --> 00:58:06.010
really like we were watching those guys goof around with fireworks.
因为他们确实在玩。

1380
00:58:06.250 --> 00:58:06.890
Because they were.
因为你们确实在玩。

1381
00:58:07.030 --> 00:58:07.870
Because you were.
因为你们确实在玩。

1382
00:58:08.670 --> 00:58:09.190
Yes.
是的。

1383
00:58:09.490 --> 00:58:10.010
Yes.
是的。

1384
00:58:10.010 --> 00:58:15.530
And after this, when we come down from the roof, you know, Jim and Pam, they leave the
在这之后，当我们从屋顶下来时，你知道，吉姆和帕姆，他们离开办公室，戴着耳机在听。

1385
00:58:15.530 --> 00:58:18.070
office and they're listening on the headphones.
哦，在14分34秒，我有个笔记写着：老式科技警报。

1386
00:58:18.390 --> 00:58:24.310
Oh, at 14 minutes, 34 seconds, I have a note card that says, old tech alert.
什么？

1387
00:58:24.870 --> 00:58:25.310
What?
因为那是iPod。

1388
00:58:25.710 --> 00:58:27.390
Because it's an iPod.
是的。

1389
00:58:27.550 --> 00:58:27.990
Yes.
那是iPod。

1390
00:58:28.130 --> 00:58:29.390
It's an iPod.
你们戴着那种小耳机，一人戴一只。

1391
00:58:29.490 --> 00:58:32.450
And you guys have like the little headphones where you each take a little ear.
太可爱了。

1392
00:58:32.650 --> 00:58:33.450
It's so cute.
嗯，马特·赫特问，在拍摇摆舞那场戏时，你和约翰到底在听什么？

1393
00:58:33.790 --> 00:58:39.210
Well, Matt Hurt asked, what, if anything, were you and John listening to when you shot the
好的。

1394
00:58:39.210 --> 00:58:40.570
swing dancing scene?
这也是我的问题之一，马特。

1395
00:58:40.770 --> 00:58:41.110
Okay.
所以到底是什么？

1396
00:58:41.210 --> 00:58:42.870
That's one of my questions too, Matt.
好的。

1397
00:58:43.070 --> 00:58:44.050
So what was it?
你在剧里听到的那首歌是特拉维斯乐队的《Sing》。

1398
00:58:44.190 --> 00:58:44.570
Okay.
但我和约翰当时其实在听一首Interpol乐队的歌。

1399
00:58:44.810 --> 00:58:49.510
The song you hear in the episode is a song called Sing by Travis.
好的。

1400
00:58:50.110 --> 00:58:54.290
But John and I were actually listening to an Interpol song.
好的。

1401
00:58:54.830 --> 00:58:55.650
Which song?
哪首歌？

1402
00:58:55.670 --> 00:58:56.470
I don't remember.
我不记得了。

1403
00:58:56.690 --> 00:58:57.890
But you know it was Interpol.
但你知道那是Interpol乐队的歌。

1404
00:58:58.010 --> 00:58:58.330
Yes.
是的。

1405
00:58:58.450 --> 00:58:59.490
I remember that.
我记得那个。

1406
00:58:59.630 --> 00:59:07.830
And I think that was John's actual iPod and that he suggested that song, that we listened
而且我觉得那是John本人的iPod，是他推荐了那首歌，我们听了

1407
00:59:07.830 --> 00:59:08.330
to the song.
那首歌。

1408
00:59:08.330 --> 00:59:10.770
Oh, Jam fans are going to love that.
噢，Jam乐队的粉丝肯定会喜欢这个。

1409
00:59:10.930 --> 00:59:11.090
Yeah.
是啊。

1410
00:59:11.250 --> 00:59:12.710
And that was also lovely.
那段也很美好。

1411
00:59:12.850 --> 00:59:14.370
Same warm summer evening.
同样温暖的夏夜。

1412
00:59:14.650 --> 00:59:15.590
It was awesome.
太棒了。

1413
00:59:15.790 --> 00:59:21.530
So we talked to Melora a little bit about the next scene, which is Michael and Jan in
所以我们和Melora聊了聊下一场戏，也就是Michael和Jan在

1414
00:59:21.530 --> 00:59:22.310
the parking lot.
停车场的那场戏。

1415
00:59:22.510 --> 00:59:24.590
That's at 15 minutes, 21 seconds.
在15分21秒处。

1416
00:59:24.870 --> 00:59:26.250
It is the big smooch.
就是那个大吻。

1417
00:59:26.370 --> 00:59:27.550
Yes, the big smooch.
没错，那个大吻。

1418
00:59:27.670 --> 00:59:27.950
All right.
好的。

1419
00:59:28.030 --> 00:59:32.290
So I feel like there's just this brilliant moment, and I don't know if it was written
我觉得这里有一个绝妙的瞬间，我不知道是剧本写的

1420
00:59:32.290 --> 00:59:39.650
or if Steve improvised this, that just shows how over the moon giddy Michael is that him
还是Steve即兴发挥的，它展现了Michael有多么欣喜若狂，因为他和

1421
00:59:39.650 --> 00:59:43.070
and Jan just kissed and that she said, let's get out of here.
Jan刚刚接吻了，而且她说，我们离开这儿吧。

1422
00:59:43.190 --> 00:59:44.110
He's so giddy.
他太兴奋了。

1423
00:59:44.230 --> 00:59:47.110
And I wrote down the scene because I thought it was so adorable.
我把这场戏记了下来，因为我觉得太可爱了。

1424
00:59:47.330 --> 00:59:49.190
It's at 15 minutes, 21 seconds.
在15分21秒处。

1425
00:59:49.670 --> 00:59:53.150
Jan says, Jan is sort of like all of a sudden camera aware, right?
Jan说，Jan好像突然意识到摄像机的存在了，对吧？

1426
00:59:53.290 --> 00:59:53.490
Yeah.
是啊。

1427
00:59:53.650 --> 00:59:54.350
She says, let's go.
她说，我们走吧。

1428
00:59:54.350 --> 00:59:55.130
She's looking for the camera.
她在找摄像机。

1429
00:59:55.230 --> 00:59:56.250
Is this getting caught on tape?
这会被拍下来吗？

1430
00:59:56.310 --> 00:59:56.430
Yeah.
是的。

1431
00:59:56.430 --> 00:59:58.310
She doesn't find the camera, but she wonders.
她没找到摄像机，但她产生了怀疑。

1432
00:59:58.590 --> 00:59:58.770
Right.
没错。

1433
00:59:58.930 --> 01:00:00.110
And so she says, let's go.
所以她说，我们走吧。

1434
01:00:00.230 --> 01:00:01.070
And Michael goes, what?
然后Michael说，什么？

1435
01:00:01.230 --> 01:00:02.210
And she goes, let's go.
她说，我们走吧。

1436
01:00:02.330 --> 01:00:03.970
And he says, where are we going?
他说，我们要去哪？

1437
01:00:04.110 --> 01:00:04.590
Oh, OK.
噢，好吧。

1438
01:00:04.770 --> 01:00:05.350
Doesn't matter.
无所谓。

1439
01:00:05.650 --> 01:00:06.490
Going to the go-go.
去跳舞吧。

1440
01:00:06.910 --> 01:00:08.270
Going to the go-go.
去跳舞吧。

1441
01:00:08.710 --> 01:00:10.170
Going to the go-go.
去跳舞吧。

1442
01:00:10.170 --> 01:00:11.810
I thought that was so cute.
我觉得那太可爱了。

1443
01:00:11.810 --> 01:00:13.650
He's just so excited.
他真是太兴奋了。

1444
01:00:13.930 --> 01:00:15.150
I thought it was adorable.
我觉得那很可爱。

1445
01:00:15.450 --> 01:00:15.750
All right.
好的。

1446
01:00:15.870 --> 01:00:17.430
So it's the next morning now.
现在是第二天早上了。

1447
01:00:17.630 --> 01:00:20.150
The Dunder Mifflin film crew enters the office.
Dunder Mifflin的摄制组进入了办公室。

1448
01:00:20.310 --> 01:00:20.990
Do they have a key?
他们有钥匙吗？

1449
01:00:21.450 --> 01:00:22.290
Do you notice that?
你注意到了吗？

1450
01:00:22.390 --> 01:00:23.810
Dwight is sleeping on the couch.
Dwight正睡在沙发上。

1451
01:00:24.070 --> 01:00:25.410
Maybe it's not even locked.
也许门根本就没锁。

1452
01:00:25.570 --> 01:00:26.130
I know.
我知道。

1453
01:00:26.130 --> 01:00:28.130
Maybe he never locked the door that night.
也许那天晚上他根本就没锁门。

1454
01:00:28.150 --> 01:00:36.070
Why is Dwight in blue underwear on his tank top under like a foil, like a FEMA foil blanket?
为什么德怀特穿着蓝色内裤，背心外面还裹着像锡纸一样的东西，那种联邦紧急事务管理局的急救毯？

1455
01:00:36.250 --> 01:00:40.810
Well, I'll tell you, there was a very big meeting about what underwear he would wear.
嗯，我告诉你，关于他该穿什么内裤，确实开过一个非常大的会议。

1456
01:00:40.970 --> 01:00:41.830
Of course there was.
当然开过。

1457
01:00:41.970 --> 01:00:42.190
Yes.
没错。

1458
01:00:42.450 --> 01:00:43.330
Would it be boxers?
是穿平角裤吗？

1459
01:00:43.410 --> 01:00:44.330
Would it be briefs?
还是三角裤？

1460
01:00:44.450 --> 01:00:45.110
What color?
什么颜色？

1461
01:00:45.310 --> 01:00:46.470
This is what they decided.
这就是他们决定的结果。

1462
01:00:46.710 --> 01:00:48.990
Of course there's a huge meeting about Dwight's underwear.
关于德怀特的内裤当然会有个大会议。

1463
01:00:49.150 --> 01:00:49.830
Of course.
当然。

1464
01:00:50.030 --> 01:00:50.230
Yeah.
是啊。

1465
01:00:50.530 --> 01:00:51.190
I know.
我知道。

1466
01:00:51.330 --> 01:00:54.670
And they decided on those blue, kind of like tighty-whities.
他们最后选了那种蓝色的，有点像紧身三角裤。

1467
01:00:55.390 --> 01:00:55.710
Yeah.
是啊。

1468
01:00:56.170 --> 01:00:58.490
They're, I guess, very slouchy.
我觉得它们看起来非常松垮。

1469
01:00:58.610 --> 01:00:59.290
Very baggy.
非常肥大。

1470
01:00:59.630 --> 01:01:01.690
Oh, you know Ray loved that.
噢，你知道雷很喜欢那样。

1471
01:01:01.830 --> 01:01:02.910
He loved every second.
他享受每一秒。

1472
01:01:03.950 --> 01:01:06.650
What about the scene where he runs to the window?
那他跑向窗户的那场戏呢？

1473
01:01:07.010 --> 01:01:08.310
Angela sees Jan.
安吉拉看到了简。

1474
01:01:08.630 --> 01:01:09.130
That's right.
没错。

1475
01:01:09.130 --> 01:01:12.650
So obviously the camera crew busts Jan, right?
所以很明显，摄影组抓到了简，对吧？

1476
01:01:12.870 --> 01:01:12.990
Yeah.
是啊。

1477
01:01:13.050 --> 01:01:13.810
She's so busted.
她彻底暴露了。

1478
01:01:13.810 --> 01:01:17.830
But there are two Dunder Mifflin employees who also now know.
但现在还有两名邓德·米夫林的员工也知道了。

1479
01:01:18.110 --> 01:01:23.450
Angela, who's arrived early in the parking lot, and Dwight, who's peeping down from the window.
提前到达停车场的安吉拉，还有从窗户往下偷窥的德怀特。

1480
01:01:23.590 --> 01:01:23.770
Yeah.
是啊。

1481
01:01:23.770 --> 01:01:25.650
And Jan sees Dwight.
而且简看到了德怀特。

1482
01:01:25.910 --> 01:01:28.210
I'm assuming she sees Angela as she drives by.
我猜她开车经过时也看到了安吉拉。

1483
01:01:28.350 --> 01:01:30.230
But I love that Dwight and Angela.
但我喜欢德怀特和安吉拉这一点。

1484
01:01:30.230 --> 01:01:31.530
Oh, I think she totally clocks you.
噢，我觉得她绝对注意到你了。

1485
01:01:31.690 --> 01:01:32.030
Oh, yeah.
噢，没错。

1486
01:01:32.090 --> 01:01:33.030
I do too.
我也这么觉得。

1487
01:01:33.030 --> 01:01:38.330
But I love that Dwight and Angela, who go on to have their secret relationship, totally busts Jan.
但我喜欢德怀特和安吉拉，他们后来发展了地下情，而且是他们彻底揭穿了简。

1488
01:01:39.510 --> 01:01:49.830
I love that it's Angela in the parking lot because I feel like the very last person who you want to see during your walk of shame is Angela.
我喜欢停车场里的人是安吉拉，因为我觉得在你感到羞愧的时候，最不想见到的人就是安吉拉。

1489
01:01:49.830 --> 01:01:51.570
Yeah, exactly.
是啊，没错。

1490
01:01:52.190 --> 01:01:52.730
All right.
好了。

1491
01:01:52.850 --> 01:01:58.030
So Michael arrives into the office with his delicious secret.
迈克尔带着他那美味的秘密来到了办公室。

1492
01:01:58.410 --> 01:01:59.430
He's so giddy.
他太兴奋了。

1493
01:01:59.570 --> 01:02:05.910
I felt like Melora described that so well, how sweet and innocent and happy he is that he –
我觉得梅洛拉描述得太好了，他那种甜蜜、天真又快乐的样子，因为他——

1494
01:02:05.910 --> 01:02:07.990
Oh, he's so excited.
噢，他太激动了。

1495
01:02:08.330 --> 01:02:08.710
So good.
太棒了。

1496
01:02:08.710 --> 01:02:11.510
And he really is like, I'm not going to talk about it, right?
他真的表现得像，我不会说出来的，对吧？

1497
01:02:11.530 --> 01:02:12.690
No, I'm not going to speak about it.
不，我不会谈论这件事。

1498
01:02:12.730 --> 01:02:14.410
He's like, gentlemen, don't kiss and tell, and neither do I.
他说，绅士从不宣扬风流韵事，我也一样。

1499
01:02:14.530 --> 01:02:14.950
Ha, ha, ha.
哈哈哈哈。

1500
01:02:15.150 --> 01:02:18.590
And then the next thing we know, he's like, we'll have to disclose.
然后下一秒，他就说，我们必须公开。

1501
01:02:18.590 --> 01:02:22.310
We'll have to write a letter about our relationship.
我们得写封信来谈谈我们的关系。

1502
01:02:22.610 --> 01:02:23.670
He just – oh, man.
他刚才——天哪。

1503
01:02:23.930 --> 01:02:26.990
In that talking head, I love the camera work in that.
在那个访谈片段里，我特别喜欢那里的运镜。

1504
01:02:27.130 --> 01:02:31.210
It's a very, very slow push in on Michael's face.
镜头非常、非常缓慢地推向迈克尔的脸。

1505
01:02:31.830 --> 01:02:37.290
And you can just feel the camera putting all this pressure on Michael to tell the truth.
你能感觉到镜头给迈克尔施加了巨大的压力，逼他说实话。

1506
01:02:37.550 --> 01:02:38.870
How long does he last?
他坚持了多久？

1507
01:02:39.050 --> 01:02:41.130
He lasts like 14 seconds.
他大概坚持了14秒。

1508
01:02:42.570 --> 01:02:44.490
He's like, all right, fine.
他就像是，好吧，行吧。

1509
01:02:44.590 --> 01:02:46.030
We went back and we –
我们回去了，然后我们——

1510
01:02:46.030 --> 01:02:46.570
To our hotel.
回到了我们的酒店。

1511
01:02:46.710 --> 01:02:48.130
Yeah, we made out for a little bit.
对，我们亲热了一会儿。

1512
01:02:48.150 --> 01:02:48.350
Made out a little.
亲热了一点点。

1513
01:02:48.590 --> 01:02:50.590
I held her and she talked to me about her divorce.
我抱着她，她跟我聊了她的离婚。

1514
01:02:50.950 --> 01:02:51.870
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1515
01:02:52.170 --> 01:02:56.150
That phone call with Jan where he goes under the desk, Greg directed that.
迈克尔躲到桌子底下接简那个电话的戏，是格雷格导演的。

1516
01:02:56.370 --> 01:03:01.750
Greg told Steve, why don't you take this phone call under the desk to avoid the camera crew?
格雷格告诉史蒂夫，你为什么不躲到桌子底下接这个电话，好避开摄像组呢？

1517
01:03:01.890 --> 01:03:07.890
And he said it was great because they were able to edit together all of Steve's improvisations
他说这招很棒，因为他们可以把史蒂夫所有的即兴发挥剪辑在一起，

1518
01:03:07.890 --> 01:03:09.970
because you can't see his mouth.
因为你根本看不见他的嘴。

1519
01:03:10.230 --> 01:03:11.710
Oh, so smart.
哦，太聪明了。

1520
01:03:11.710 --> 01:03:17.470
Yeah, because Steve was improvising a lot of that phone call and the things that, you know, he was saying back to Jan.
是啊，因为史蒂夫在那个电话里即兴发挥了很多内容，还有他回应简的那些话。

1521
01:03:18.450 --> 01:03:22.830
Then we have Jim and Pam's – whew, kind of their first fight.
然后是吉姆和帕姆的——呼，算是他们的第一次争吵吧。

1522
01:03:23.310 --> 01:03:23.890
I don't know.
我不知道。

1523
01:03:23.890 --> 01:03:27.530
I mean, they have that hiccup at the dojo, but this is different.
我是说，他们在道场有过一点小摩擦，但这回不一样。

1524
01:03:27.750 --> 01:03:28.910
They have little moments.
他们之间有过一些小插曲。

1525
01:03:28.910 --> 01:03:34.130
I mean, he got his feelings really hurt when you suggested he try – you know, go for that job at the other branch.
我是说，当你建议他去尝试——你知道，去争取分部那个职位时，他真的受伤了。

1526
01:03:34.130 --> 01:03:37.010
And then there was the dojo, and now there's this.
然后是道场那次，现在又是这次。

1527
01:03:37.910 --> 01:03:41.290
Well, this one doesn't get resolved at the end of this episode.
嗯，这一集结束时，这件事还没解决。

1528
01:03:41.890 --> 01:03:46.870
Jim suggests to Pam that maybe they had their first date, that you could say this was their first date.
吉姆暗示帕姆，也许他们刚才约会了，你可以说这就是他们的第一次约会。

1529
01:03:46.890 --> 01:03:48.030
And I want to say something.
我想说点什么。

1530
01:03:48.310 --> 01:03:52.090
I understand why Pam bristles at this.
我理解为什么帕姆对这一点感到反感。

1531
01:03:52.090 --> 01:03:53.990
Well, let me just take a minute.
好吧，让我花点时间理一理。

1532
01:03:54.270 --> 01:04:00.110
First of all, Pam lies to Roy, bold-faced lies to Roy and says, I have to stay at work.
首先，帕姆对罗伊撒了谎，公然对罗伊撒谎说，我得留在公司加班。

1533
01:04:00.250 --> 01:04:02.130
And he's like, are you kidding me right now?
而罗伊的反应是，你现在是在跟我开玩笑吗？

1534
01:04:02.190 --> 01:04:03.750
And she's like, no, I have to work.
她却说，没有，我得工作。

1535
01:04:04.010 --> 01:04:10.910
So already, like, she has probably within her moral compass stepped over a line.
所以，在她的道德准则范围内，她可能已经越界了。

1536
01:04:10.910 --> 01:04:17.030
I think for Jim – now look, guys, I'm a huge Jim and Pam fan, and I wanted them together from the beginning.
我觉得对吉姆来说——听着，伙计们，我是吉姆和帕姆的超级粉丝，我从一开始就希望他们在一起。

1537
01:04:17.030 --> 01:04:24.350
But I would think as a guy – like, I was talking to my husband about this, and he goes, this is kind of a move what Jim's doing.
但作为一个男人，我会想——我跟我丈夫聊过这个，他说，吉姆这招有点心机。

1538
01:04:24.590 --> 01:04:26.590
You know, he knows she has a fiancé.
你知道，他明知她有未婚夫。

1539
01:04:26.690 --> 01:04:26.850
Yeah.
没错。

1540
01:04:27.030 --> 01:04:31.090
But he makes a grilled cheese sandwich, takes her up on the roof.
但他做了个烤奶酪三明治，把她带到了屋顶。

1541
01:04:31.230 --> 01:04:32.210
Like, he knows.
你看，他心里清楚。

1542
01:04:32.290 --> 01:04:33.590
He knows this is his moment.
他知道这就是他的机会。

1543
01:04:33.750 --> 01:04:34.830
He's going for it.
他要主动出击了。

1544
01:04:35.710 --> 01:04:37.910
Ultimately, they end up together, so it's great.
最终他们确实在一起了，所以这很好。

1545
01:04:38.150 --> 01:04:42.530
But that's not – that kind of breaks guy code of what you do with someone else's fiancé.
但这并不是——这有点违背了男人之间关于如何对待别人未婚妻的准则。

1546
01:04:42.990 --> 01:04:47.510
Well, and then I think for him to call it out so clearly out in the open,
嗯，而且我觉得他把这件事说得那么直白，摆到了台面上，

1547
01:04:47.950 --> 01:04:56.390
I think Pam is willing to pretend like none of that is happening and they're just friends while it's happening.
我觉得帕姆本来愿意假装这一切都没发生，在事情进行时只把对方当朋友。

1548
01:04:57.070 --> 01:05:05.490
But for you to just look at her and say, hey, you were kind of unfaithful last night was very shocking for her, and she had to shut that down.
但你直接看着她说，嘿，你昨晚有点不忠，这对她来说太震惊了，她必须立刻制止。

1549
01:05:05.630 --> 01:05:06.550
She had to be like, I'm sorry.
她不得不说，抱歉。

1550
01:05:06.550 --> 01:05:07.970
I don't know what you're talking about.
我不知道你在说什么。

1551
01:05:08.110 --> 01:05:09.030
You're just my friend.
你只是我的朋友。

1552
01:05:09.590 --> 01:05:11.530
And we were hanging out after work.
我们只是下班后一起聚聚。

1553
01:05:11.530 --> 01:05:14.990
So I don't know what you thought that was, but uncool.
所以我不知道你是怎么想的，但这很不地道。

1554
01:05:15.450 --> 01:05:15.930
Right.
没错。

1555
01:05:16.050 --> 01:05:23.430
That was her way of trying to get her boundary back and also just being defensive knowing that she did something she shouldn't have, I think.
我觉得那是她试图重申界限的方式，同时也因为知道自己做了不该做的事而进行自我防御。

1556
01:05:23.550 --> 01:05:30.990
Well, I think whenever, like, there's a moment when Angela catches her with Pam Pong, then Meredith catches the shirt coming up, right?
嗯，我觉得每当安吉拉撞见她和帕姆打乒乓球，或者梅雷迪斯看到她撩起衬衫的时候，对吧？

1557
01:05:30.990 --> 01:05:37.210
And then this moment when he calls it out, all of those moments are when Pam gets a mirror held up to her behavior,
还有当他指出这一点的时候，所有这些时刻都是帕姆在面对自己行为的一面镜子，

1558
01:05:37.210 --> 01:05:45.170
and it makes her uncomfortable because she knows the right thing to do is say, Roy, I'm in love with Jim, and we should break up.
这让她感到不舒服，因为她知道正确做法应该是告诉罗伊，我爱上了吉姆，我们应该分手。

1559
01:05:45.330 --> 01:05:45.490
Yeah.
是啊。

1560
01:05:45.490 --> 01:05:53.130
But she's got all of these layers like you do in a relationship and feelings probably of guilt and obligation and all of that all wrapped up into it,
但她就像你在一段关系中一样，背负着各种包袱，可能还有内疚感和责任感，所有这些都交织在一起，

1561
01:05:53.210 --> 01:05:54.930
so she doesn't know how to make that break.
所以她不知道该如何做出那个了断。

1562
01:05:55.150 --> 01:05:55.390
Yeah.
没错。

1563
01:05:55.550 --> 01:06:00.770
And I think this is one of those moments where a mirror is held up, and she feels bad, and she bristles at it.
我觉得这就是那种让她照镜子的时刻，她感到难受，并对此感到抵触。

1564
01:06:00.850 --> 01:06:05.950
And then it all ends with that final look between Michael and Jim, the little shrug.
最后以迈克尔和吉姆之间的那个眼神交流结束，那个小小的耸肩。

1565
01:06:06.670 --> 01:06:07.550
Eh, women.
唉，女人啊。

1566
01:06:07.830 --> 01:06:09.110
Ah, what are you going to do?
啊，能怎么办呢？

